Based on the context provided, when a streaming resume attempt fails with HTTP 409 (checkpoint mismatch), the server's error payload includes the following JSON schema:

```json
{
  "title": "Error Payload",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "status": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "HTTP status code",
      "minimum": 400,
      "maximum": 599
    },
    "error": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Error message",
      "minLength": 1
    },
    "resume_details": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Additional resume details",
      "properties": {
        "truncation_preview": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Truncated preview of the stream data",
          "minLength": 1
        },
        "prefix_hash": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Hash of the prefix of the stream data",
          "minLength": 1
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "required": ["status", "error"]
}
```

The `kv_crc` value inside v2 resume tokens is computed using the CRC32 algorithm. The algorithm takes the binary representation of the data as input and produces a 32-bit checksum as output. The checksum is then encoded in base64 and included in the resume token as a string.
